{title: You Are My Son}
{subtitle: Psalms 2:7–8}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] [C] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The One enthroned in heaven [Bb]laughs
He mocks the [C]raging kings [Dm]below
Then he speaks in anger [Bb]and wrath
Terri[Gm]fying [Am7]them as they [Dm]go
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
I my[Bb]self have in[C]stalled my [Dm]king
Up[Bb]on Zion my [C]holy [Dm]mountain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You are my Son today I [Bb]have begotten [F]you
[Gm]Ask of me and [Dm]I will [C]make the nations [A]yours
[Dm]The ends of the earth shall [Bb]be your posses[F]sion
[Gm]You are [Dm]my Son today [C]I have [A]begotten [Dm]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Break them with an iron rod
[Bb]Shatter them [C]like a potter's [Dm]jar
So now be wise you kings [Bb]of earth
Be warned [Gm]you jud[A]ges far and [Dm]near
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Serve the [C]Lord with [Dm]fear
Re[Bb]joice with [C]trem[A]bling
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Dm]You are my Son today I [Bb]have begotten [F]you
[Gm]Ask of me and [Dm]I will [C]make the nations [A]yours
[Dm]The ends of the earth shall [Bb]be your posses[F]sion
[Gm]You are [Dm]my Son today [C]I have [A]begotten [Dm]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I will proclaim the Lord's decree
You are my Son
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
